---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const description = 'A native macOS utility combining a launcher, dictation, clipboard history, snippets and window switching.';
const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "SoftwareApplication",
  "@id": "https://marijnbent.nl/ollie/#app",
  "name": "Ollie",
  "url": "https://github.com/marijnbent/ollie",
  "description": description,
  "applicationCategory": "ProductivityApplication",
  "operatingSystem": "macOS 26 or later",
  "author": {
    "@type": "Person",
    "@id": "https://marijnbent.nl/#person",
    "name": "Marijn Bent",
    "url": "https://marijnbent.nl/"
  }
};
---

<Layout title="Ollie – Marijn Bent" description={description} schema={schema} emoji="🦦">
  <article class="prose-content">
    <div class="space-y-4 leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        Ollie brings the small tools I use throughout the day into one native macOS app. VibeScribe’s dictation is now part of it, alongside an app launcher, clipboard history, text snippets and window switching.
      </p>
      <p>
        Use the keyboard to open apps, find something you copied earlier or insert a saved snippet. For dictation, hold a shortcut, speak and insert the transcript into the app you’re using, with optional AI cleanup.
      </p>
      <p>
        Ollie also includes desktop switching, camera imports, ntfy notifications, typing sounds and per-app network usage. Each feature can be enabled separately, with shared shortcut settings and a compact menu bar interface.
      </p>
      <p>
        The launcher builds on Tinycast. Ollie is open source and requires macOS 26 or later. The code and build instructions are on <a href="https://github.com/marijnbent/ollie" class="text-foreground font-medium underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-foreground/80 transition-colors">GitHub</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
